# Directories .vercelignore already excludes wholesale — each is a
# standalone tool/repo folded into this monorepo, with its build output
# committed separately under public/ (flow-design/ -> public/flow-design/,
# codeflow/ -> public/codeflow/, Git Visualizer/ -> public/git-visualizer/
# via `npm run build:git`). temp/ and scratch/ are just dev scratch files.
#
# They used to be git-tracked despite being .vercelignore-excluded, which
# breaks Vercel's deploy: it removes each directory early in the build per
# .vercelignore, then a later "Deploying outputs" step re-walks the full
# git-tracked file list and fails with "ENOENT: no such file or directory,
# lstat '.../codeflow/card/action.yml'" (or any other file inside) because
# the directory it's looking for is already gone. Untracking them — not
# just their own nested .gitignore files, every file — is what avoids
# tripping this path entirely. Reproduced and confirmed fixed locally via
# a clean clone + `vercel build && vercel deploy --prebuilt`.
/flow-design/
/Git Visualizer/
/codeflow/
/temp/
/scratch/

# Data
dsa_data.txt
dsa_data_*.txt
.angular/

# Orphaned root-level duplicates of the same scraped course content (one
# raw JSON, one wrapped as `window.courseData = …`), unreferenced by any
# app code — the only mention was a defensive vercel.json excludeFiles
# entry that stopped them from being bundled into serverless functions but
# didn't stop them from being uploaded as static deployment assets. Two
# 14 MB files with no consumer is exactly the kind of single object that
# trips Vercel's per-file upload limit ("Request body too large. Limit:
# 10mb"). `course 1.html`, a local preview scratch file, references
# differently-named siblings (`course_data.js`, `scraped_data 2.json`)
# that don't even exist here, confirming none of this is wired up.
/scraped_data.json
/course_data 1.js


# Ignore AFFiNE embedded repo
AFFiNE/

# Upstream samples repo used only as build input for the AgentCore samples
# viewer (scripts/build_agentcore_samples.py). The generated output that
# actually ships lives in public/agentcore-samples/.
agentcore-samples-main/

# Upstream sources used only as build input for the LangChain docs viewer
# (scripts/build_langchain_docs.py) — together about 1.1 GB.
# Leading slashes matter: an unanchored `Langchain/` also matches
# `public/langchain/` on a case-insensitive filesystem, which would silently
# drop the shipped docs.
/LangChain-website/
/Langchain/
/Claude Certeficate/

# Upstream curriculum used only as build input for the AI from Scratch viewer
# (scripts/build_ai_from_scratch.py) — 19 MB of lesson sources. What ships is
# the sanitized output under public/ai-from-scratch/, which is itself served
# from R2 like the other doc archives below.
/ai-engineering-from-scratch-main/

# Generated output of build_agentcore_samples.py, build_langchain_docs.py,
# build_strands_docs.py and build_manual_data.py — ~234 MB / ~9,980 files
# across the AgentCore docs+samples, LangChain docs, Strands docs and guides
# viewers. Previously committed here and shipped as static files, which is
# what pushed the Vercel deployment manifest over its request-body limit
# ("Request body too large. Limit: 10mb") starting with the commit that added
# public/codelab/. Now served from R2 by docs-cdn-worker/, reached through the
# vercel.json rewrites for these five paths — same-origin from the browser's
# point of view, so no code changes were needed. Re-upload after regenerating
# with: node scripts/upload_docs_archive.mjs
/public/agentcore-samples/
/public/agentcore/
/public/langchain/
/public/strands/
/public/guides/
/public/ai-from-scratch/

# Third-party clone (github.com/Garvit244/Leetcode) carrying its own git
# history. Git can only store it as a submodule pointer, which clones as an
# empty folder, so it is excluded rather than committed broken.
/Leetcode/

# Raw scraped/build-input data for the AlgoWar arena and codelab dataset.
# The generated output that ships lives in src/data/codelab/ and
# public/codelab/, which ARE committed.
/Algowar/
/dsanew/

